[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue because the subject lines matched
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). The reports hold two problems with two
different fixes. Both flip a date's month and day for tenants that write the day first.

<Callout>
Not one issue. The parser fix queued for #4471 does not reach the second problem.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Each report is placed by its tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`), not by the tag intake
guessed from the reporter's browser. The two disagree on some reports, so a count by intake tag is
wrong. The export repeats some reports; the table counts each id once.

## The two problems

1. **`parser`: dates are read month first.** The shared parser reads every date month first.
   Ticket: [issue 1](https://github.com/arkdru23/what-it-shows/issues/1). Fix: read dates by the
   tenant's locale.
2. **`hint`: the booking-v3 form hint is month first.** The form prints a month-first hint under
   its date field. People at day-first tenants type what the hint says, and the form reads it
   day first. Ticket: [issue 2](https://github.com/arkdru23/what-it-shows/issues/2). Fix: change
   the hint the form prints. A parser fix does not touch it.

## Lessons

- Merging on the subject line joined reports whose causes differ. Count the cause, not the subject.
- A tag guessed at intake is a guess. The tenant says which cause a report has.
- A number that can be computed is computed: the table above is built from the data.

